{"id": "EUVD-2026-80598", "enisaUuid": "54d5c191-9d00-330b-8798-575ee2117233", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nceph: lock mutex in ceph_mds_check_access()\n\nMDS session OPEN handling replaces mdsc->s_cap_auths under\nmdsc->mutex, freeing the previous array and its strings.\n\nceph_mds_check_access() traverses this array without holding the\nmutex.  A concurrent session reopen can therefore free the array while\nit is being inspected, resulting in a use-after-free like this:\n\n  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 003aaad64b2c8bb9\n  [...]\n  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000004 [#1]  SMP\n  Modules linked in:\n  CPU: 56 UID: 2953037534 PID: 1253231 Comm: php-cgi8.4 Not tainted 6.18.45-i2-ampere #1146 NONE\n  [..]\n  pc : ceph_mds_check_access+0xd4/0x550\n  lr : ceph_mds_check_access+0xc8/0x550\n  [...]\n  Call trace:\n   ceph_mds_check_access+0xd4/0x550 (P)\n   ceph_atomic_open+0x138/0xbe8\n   path_openat+0xa24/0xfa8\n   do_filp_open+0x94/0x158\n   do_sys_openat2+0x88/0xf8", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:04", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/729c1ff670ece6f3d4b1738365a0b2f90d487523", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca5bfea2045ef2eb3305cf2a9d8da549b76c37d3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df1a97d5313fccadb08390306d49b194fb027392", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a61c6ae1dae2611082b831b4aaa780878099c012"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pccj-hx6x-mqg3", "CVE-2026-89990"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.61, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46a9fcd8-2635-361d-a8db-bc72f300dcb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "577c6ef1-7441-3178-b859-eea52f35ae21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "57f5061b-d3fd-3488-824c-551217831da8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "596afb0b8933ba6ed7227adcc538db26feb25c74 <a61c6ae1dae2611082b831b4aaa780878099c012"}, {"id": "64715997-e017-3d4e-937a-3d06622b483d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "596afb0b8933ba6ed7227adcc538db26feb25c74 <729c1ff670ece6f3d4b1738365a0b2f90d487523"}, {"id": "8456454d-79a1-37cd-bd16-f07fea1250ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "9826e4ce-1df3-3e4c-9d49-d82372f9e475", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "b3310ca6-ae7d-3944-a79f-7aba33dbdd71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "d0439e46-d3a3-3199-a711-7ed153aa78fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "596afb0b8933ba6ed7227adcc538db26feb25c74 <df1a97d5313fccadb08390306d49b194fb027392"}, {"id": "d7c22e90-0579-330e-ba09-a72e679a26bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "596afb0b8933ba6ed7227adcc538db26feb25c74 <ca5bfea2045ef2eb3305cf2a9d8da549b76c37d3"}, {"id": "ee1e8b74-1c15-3002-b578-1d9dea73c5b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "10ce1855-9463-3828-b865-3573c672f092", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}